<title>JAPAN: Enix shares up on game software plans.</title>
<headline>Enix shares up on game software plans.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Enix Corp was higher in early morning trade on Thursday, energised by news that it would develop and supply the latest version of one of its popular videogame software packages to Sony Corp, brokers said.</p>
<p>As of 0043 GMT, the shares stood at 2,950 yen in the over-the-counter market, up from 2,750 yen on Tuesday. Markets were closed Wednesday for a national holiday.  </p>
<p>Media reports on Wednesday said that Enix, which in the past supplied Nintendo Co Ltd with Dragon Quest software, would develop the new version exclusively for Sony.</p>
<p>The reports could not immediately be confirmed.</p>
<p>Nintendo shares were down 380 yen at 7,620 yen.</p>
</text>
